  "scope": "Actual source-bound CPU Adam/TBPTT updates on two fixed Rust-admitted synthetic graphs, four adjacent order-balanced pairs per graph and platform, two Torch CPU threads. The previous compensated implementation is restored from its exact snapshot; the candidate is the current module. Batched Float32 partials, an error-corrected tree and analytic Float32 adjoints reduce update time while retaining original-input autograd views. Standard/wide optimizer gates, original frozen failing export, CUDA trained-export equality and independent accuracy/gradient tests retain the original numeric limits. Short CPU/CUDA rows stay direct. Shared-host aggregates do not establish an idle host, game step timing, maturity, integrated capacity or a full soak.",
